// Demonstration of the `flowchart` package — program flowcharts as a thin layer of
// conventions over the diagram layer.
//
// Render with:  texish scripts/flowchart-demo.script

\use{flowchart}

\def headline {\italic{The flowchart package} \hfil page \the\pageno}
\def footline {\hfil — \the\pageno — \hfil}
\set raggedbottom {1}
\def centerline c {\hbox to:\hsize {\hfil\c\hfil}}

\font lmroman 12 regular

\bold{Program flowcharts}

The flowchart package names the diagram shapes by their roles — a \italic{terminal} for
start and stop, a \italic{process} rectangle, a \italic{decision} diamond, a
\italic{parallelogram} for input and output — and reads the edges as flow. Below, the
sum $\sum_{i=1}^{n} i$ is computed with a counting loop: the decision branches \italic{yes}
down into the loop body, which curves back to test again, and \italic{no} across to the
output.

\vskip 10pt

\centerline{\picture width:4.4in height:5in {
  \start{begin}{at 1.5in 4.6in}{Start}
  \io{read}{below begin}{Read $n$}
  \process{init}{below read}{$s \gets 0,\quad i \gets 1$}
  \decision{test}{below init}{$i \le n$?}
  \process{body}{below test 46}{$s \gets s + i,\quad i \gets i + 1$}
  \io{out}{right test 96}{Print $s$}
  \stop{done}{below out}{Stop}

  \flow{begin}{read}
  \flow{read}{init}
  \flow{init}{test}
  \flow[yes]{test}{body}
  \cedge[58]{body}{test}{}
  \flow[no]{test}{out}
  \flow{out}{done}
}}
